# Commit peak with a 50k database queue live (#109, design 1.3 M6; the
# 16-A "commit with a 50k queue live" case): as commit-peak-50k.script,
# but Songs row 0 plays first (snapshot_play: lib_play() of all 50,000
# rows, indices[] and the slot table ~406 KB held) and stops; the update
# then commits with the queue still current. The peak margin is the
# "floor_watch commit_peak free" minimum against the 7.5 MB floor (32 MB),
# and the queue is rebased after the publication (dbq rebase).
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui32 SIMDISK=<a clone of build/sim-50k/simdisk> \
#     scripts/shots.sh tests/perf/commit-peak-dbq-50k.script
# golden: skip published
# fulls-extra: 2 snapshot_play pushes Now Playing and the stop returns
# log: dbq build n=
# log: dbq rebase block=

wait 4000
wait_db 300000
snapshot_play
wait 3000
audio_stop
wait 1000
snapshot_stress_begin
floor_watch begin timeline
copy ../../tests/ui/fixtures/refresh.mp3 /zz-commit-peak.mp3
update_db
expect_snapshot_stress_switch 300000
floor_watch end commit_peak free
shot published
wait 3000                  # the rebase runs at the thread's next pass
quit
